# Build-context ignore rules for iris/Dockerfile.
#
# The iris image is built with the repo root as the context (it COPYs both
# `iris/` and its sibling `memiris/`). The repo-root .dockerignore, however, is
# scoped to the logos build — it ignores everything except `logos/*` to keep
# that image slim (see #682). Applied to the iris build it empties the context,
# so every COPY fails with "not found".
#
# BuildKit prefers a `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile over the
# context-root `.dockerignore`, so these rules apply to the iris build only and
# leave the logos context untouched. Patterns are relative to the context root
# (the repo root). Keep only what iris/Dockerfile needs, minus caches/VCS noise.
*
!iris
!memiris

**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.git
**/node_modules
